    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "After the high-stakes medical entrance exam on May 3, an anonymous tipster from a small city sent proof that the chemistry paper had leaked. The testing authority received the evidence and passed the case to national investigators. This led to the exam being invalidated, giving the millions of honest students who prepared fairly another chance on June 21.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Everyman",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-0",
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "result-0",
          "result-2"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.88
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "The crackdown following the leaked exam paper reached the workers behind the test, with over two dozen exam contractors turned over for investigation. Among those held accountable was a public figure who had once championed student justice, now accused of compromising the system's integrity. The consequence for the broader group was immediate arrest.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Everyman",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-2",
          "how-3",
          "result-1"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.82
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "While thirteen people face the immediate consequence of arrest, the retest arranged for June 21 throws the entire burden back on the students. The examination's cancellation means months of preparation are thrown away for everyone, forcing them to retake a stressful assessment they did not break. It's a rescheduling that feels more like punishment than a second chance.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Everyman",
        "fragments": [
          "result-0",
          "how-4",
          "result-2"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.75
    }
  ],
